@startuml geo-cell-write
title US-12: Geo-Cell Write - Historical Index + Live Redis Spatial Membership

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\nadsb.raw / ais.raw" as Kafka
participant "Position\nConsumer" as Consumer
database "Redis\nentity:live:{id}" as LiveState
database "Redis\ngeo-cell:{cell}\n(sorted set)" as GeoCell
database "TimescaleDB\nposition_history" as TSDB
queue "Kafka\nposition.normalized" as Normalized

Kafka -> Consumer : consume raw event\n{ entity_id, lat, lon, timestamp_ms, ... }
Consumer -> Consumer : normalize + compute\nhistory_geo_cell = H3(..., HISTORY_H3_RESOLUTION)\nlive_geo_cell = H3(..., LIVE_H3_RESOLUTION)

Consumer -> LiveState : read stored last_seen_ms + live_geo_cell
LiveState --> Consumer : previous state or nil

alt incoming.timestamp_ms < stored.last_seen_ms
  Consumer -> Consumer : stale/out-of-order event\ndo not regress Redis live state or geo-cell membership
else event accepted for live state
  alt previous live_geo_cell exists AND changed
    Consumer -> GeoCell : ZREM geo-cell:{old_live_geo_cell} entity_id
  end

  Consumer -> GeoCell : ZADD geo-cell:{new_live_geo_cell}\nscore=timestamp_ms member=entity_id
  Consumer -> LiveState : HSET latest position + last_seen_ms + live_geo_cell\nrefresh 24h safety TTL
end

Consumer -> TSDB : INSERT position_history\n(entity_id, observed_at, timestamp_ms, geo_cell=history_geo_cell, ...)\nON CONFLICT (entity_id, observed_at) DO NOTHING

note over TSDB
  Hypertable partitions by observed_at only.
  geo_cell is an indexed column used to narrow rows
  inside selected time chunks.
  There is no TimescaleDB chunk per H3 cell.
end note

Consumer -> Normalized : publish accepted canonical event\n{ entity_id, timestamp_ms, history_geo_cell, live_geo_cell, ... }

note over GeoCell
  Sorted-set score is last_seen_ms.
  Correlation Worker uses ZRANGEBYSCORE
  across the current cell + computed k-ring.
  Stale members age out logically by score.
end note

@enduml
